      <main class="site-main site-main--home">
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="hero__media" aria-hidden="true">
            <img
              src="/assets/images/playerimages/UserOptcron-2.webp"
              alt=""
              width="1920"
              height="1080"
              fetchpriority="high"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="hero__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="hero__content">
            <div class="hero__inner">
              <img
                class="hero__brand"
                src="/assets/branding/logo.svg"
                alt="Commonwealth Online"
                width="2783"
                height="685"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <h1 id="hero-title">Fallout 4 multiplayer, built from the ground up.</h1>
              <p class="hero__tagline">
                Connect to a dedicated server and share the Commonwealth with other players. Version 1.1.0 adds
                invite-based internet hosting through Iroh, a full graphical host workflow, stronger controller support,
                and optional public server discovery alongside the existing player sync and shared world state.
              </p>
              <div class="hero__actions">
                <a class="co-btn co-btn--primary" href="#" data-co-link="nexus">Download mod</a>
                <a class="co-btn co-btn--ghost" href="#" data-co-link="discord">Join Discord</a>
                <a class="co-btn co-btn--ghost" href="/media">Browse Media</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="media-credit hero__credit">Supplied by Optcron on Discord</span>
        </section>

        <section class="site-section overview" id="overview">
          <p class="section-kicker">Overview</p>
          <h2>Shared-world Fallout, one system at a time</h2>
          <p>
            Commonwealth Online is a multiplayer framework for Fallout 4, supporting both the Anniversary Edition and
            the original release. Multiple players connect to a dedicated server and share the Commonwealth while each
            client continues to run its own copy of the game. The framework synchronises movement, appearance,
            equipment, world time, weather and session data between those games.
          </p>
          <p>
            The project has grown well beyond a prototype: dedicated servers, remote player replication, equipment
            sync, shared world state, private internet hosting, authenticated public listings, password protection and
            host moderation controls are all functional. Independent fan project. Not affiliated with Bethesda or Microsoft.
          </p>
          <ul class="overview__stack" aria-label="Runtime stack">
            <li><span>Game</span><strong>Fallout 4 (Anniversary Edition &amp; original)</strong></li>
            <li><span>Client</span><strong>F4SE plugin (per-player simulation)</strong></li>
            <li><span>Server</span><strong>Python relay + graphical host + Iroh internet transport</strong></li>
            <li><span>UI</span><strong>PrismaUI / HTML menus (PrismaUI installed separately)</strong></li>
            <li><span>Status</span><strong>Actively developed, core multiplayer systems functional</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="site-section requirements" id="requirements">
          <p class="section-kicker">Requirements</p>
          <h2>Anniversary Edition and the original release, both supported</h2>
          <p>
            Commonwealth Online runs on both Fallout 4 Anniversary Edition and the original release. You can join a
            server from either version of the game, alongside players using the other.
          </p>
          <p>
            DLC, mods and Creation Club content are not required to join or play. You only need optional content when
            other players in the same session are using it. For example, so their apparel, weapons or world assets can
            resolve on your client.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="site-section features" id="features">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker">Features</p>
            <h2>Current, active and planned systems</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-subsection">
            <h3 class="feature-subsection__title">Current</h3>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Dedicated Multiplayer Servers</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">External dedicated server with multiple clients, world-state sync, JSON config and local or remote hosting.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Visible Remote Players</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Runtime proxy actors with synchronised position, rotation, cell and worldspace transitions.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Movement &amp; Animation</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Idle and movement state, sprinting, sneaking, jumping, weapon-drawn state and teleports.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Character Appearance</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Body morphs, tints, hair, head parts, facial sliders and versioned optional data.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Clothing &amp; Equipment</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Equipped apparel mirrored across tracked slots, including changes while standing still.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Ranged Weapon Sync</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Right-hand weapons with local form resolution, proxy equipping and drawn/holstered state.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Shared Time &amp; Weather</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">In-game time, days passed, exterior weather and corrections after menus and loading.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Server Browser</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Public Browse, LAN discovery, favourites, recent servers, TCP Direct Connect, Iroh invite-code Direct Connect, password prompts and full controller navigation.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Internet Hosting via Iroh</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Host from a home PC without router port forwarding or a public IPv4 address. Share an invite code privately or opt into the public server list.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Graphical Host &amp; Moderation</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">World name, player limit, private/public visibility, invite code, password protection, connection-path status, connected-player list, kick, ban and unban controls.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Custom Main Menu</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">HTML menu via PrismaUI with multiplayer access, embedded browser, settings and input capture.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Server-Based Characters</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Per-server saves, in-game character creation and profile binding on reconnect.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Development &amp; Hosting Tools</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">End-user graphical host, CLI relay, graphical dev server, fake clients, weather controls, authenticated directory tooling and deployment scripts.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-subsection">
            <h3 class="feature-subsection__title">In active development</h3>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Expanded Player Capacity</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Architecture targets ~16 players long-term with better proxy allocation and performance.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Animation Refinement</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Armed locomotion, draw/holster transitions, firing, melee, strafing and jump recovery.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Weapon &amp; Combat Actions</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Firing, reloading, melee, grenades, aiming, hit reactions and death/revival events.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Multiplayer Settings</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Profile, voice, map/social, network and keybind options with persistent configuration.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Fallout 4 Settings Bridge</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Open original Scaleform settings over the Commonwealth Online UI.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Custom Pause Menu &amp; Map</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Zoom, pan, player markers and settings panels connected to live game data.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Expanded Server Administration</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Build on the shipped kick, ban, unban, password and session controls with richer permissions, remote administration and operator tooling.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-subsection">
            <h3 class="feature-subsection__title">Planned</h3>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Multiplayer Map &amp; Markers</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Local and remote players, friends, locations, quests and custom markers.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Player Profiles &amp; Gamertags</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Display names, icons, per-server characters, friends and optional account links.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Voice &amp; Text Chat</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Proximity voice, party channels, server text chat, DMs and muting.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Teams &amp; Social Features</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Parties, shared markers, invitations and group voice/text channels.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Interaction Sync</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Doors, containers, terminals, workbenches, pickups and dialogue with shared vs local rules.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Enemy &amp; NPC Sync</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Shared enemy positions, combat state, health, death, loot and basic AI coordination.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Quest &amp; World Progression</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Selected quest stages, discovery, cleared locations, workshops and world-state changes.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Settlement Building</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Cooperative construction with shared objects, resources, ownership and persistence.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Power Armour</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Enter/exit frames, equipped pieces, fusion cores, movement and repair sync.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Trading &amp; Inventory</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Player trading, transfers, dropped items, shared containers and validation.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Mod Compatibility</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Load-order checks, version negotiation and missing-content warnings when peers use DLC, mods or Creation Club assets you do not have.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="feature-list__name">Expanded Public Server Infrastructure</span>
                <span class="feature-list__desc">Extend the working authenticated public directory with regions, richer filtering, moderation policy and larger-scale operational tooling.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

